Wrap up and end a call at the CRM's ceiling; drop the line's sales rules on demo calls.

Applies to /opt/fanum-voice/fanum-voice-core.py on the PBX, as it stands since
2026-10-16 07:28 UTC (the explicit-language change: Azerbaijani by default,
another language only on the caller's explicit request). Built on 50dc8af7
first and merged onto it; a demo script keeps EXPLICIT_LANGUAGE_POLICY, and a
demo call's ask-repeat after a fresh recovery has az/ru/en/tr neutral wording.

  before: 80292277924ec452586357d73ddc20665ae76b24f5668bf806698514fd007b63
  after:  e38400b8d339f94b78c60f44c70e3cdcac5ed71269614c3be08c0d086bd94386

- call-continuation `maxSeconds` (30-900) arms one deadline per call, counted
  from the AudioSocket connect. In the last 20 s (never later than -8 s) the
  agent is told to wrap up: in the first 4 s of that window only once the
  floor has stayed free for 1.5 s, then at the first free moment.
- The call ends through begin_hangup + AudioSocket close, so Handler.finally
  posts the transcript exactly once:
  - 1.5 s after a goodbye has played in full - the reply to the wrap-up, or
    on a demo call the agent's own closing (call-continuation `closingKeys`,
    one per language, matched with spaces out) - or after any later answer;
  - 3 s after the caller spoke following a goodbye they heard in full, when
    the model says nothing;
  - at the cap.
  A goodbye cut by the caller, interrupted by a provider reconnect, or whose
  queued audio playback dropped is not "done". On a capped call, transcript
  text arriving after turnComplete with no reply owed stays in the closed
  turn (a new item for it would retarget playback and cut the goodbye); a
  text-only item that still appears holds neither the floor nor the goodbye.
- A continuation answer that was lost (timeout, transport) or still on its
  way after 10 s is asked once more, off the greeting path, for the ceiling.
- `variant: "demo"` drops CALL_SCOPE / CALL_QUALIFICATION /
  STRUCTURED_MEASUREMENT (or uses the CRM's demo `prompt` instead of the
  line's), keeps the two delivery policies, and words recovery without
  "measurement". A call-less runtime-config answer marked `variant: "demo"`
  serves that call only and is never cached.
- Both CRM requests say `caps=demo-v1`: the CRM then never guesses a demo
  call for a call-less prompt request. The call result says
  `demoPromptApplied: true` only for a demo call that ran on the demo script.
Ordinary calls: same prompt, same events, same payload (checked against the
live core over 51 comparisons); the call-less request URL gains
`?caps=demo-v1`, and a lost continuation answer is asked once more.
Deploy order: the CRM change (runtime-config honours caps, call-continuation
sends variant/prompt/closingKeys, call-result accepts demoPromptApplied)
first; then this core.
